rn0search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; For a cone of reals $x$, the reals of $\\mathrm{HOD}^{L[x]}$ are precisely the reals in $Q_3$, or equivalently, the set of reals in $M_1$, the minimal proper class mouse with a Woodin cardinal. We show that if $z$ is any real coding $M_1|δ^{+M_1}$, then $z$ is the base of such a cone (so $M_1^{#}$ is such a base). ... This paper proves asymptotically optimal linear degree lower bounds for Nullstellensatz and Polynomial Calculus, yielding a four-way polynomial-versus-exponential proof-size classification for uniform polynomial consequences over fields of positive characteristic.\n\nThe Cone Fixing the Reals of $\\mathrm{HOD}^{M_{2n}(x)}\n\nFarmer Schlutzenberg, Connor Watson\n\narXiv:2611.06032\n\nAuthors: Farmer Schlutzenberg, Connor Watson\n\nSubmitted: Nov 2026 | Updated: Nov 2026\n\nFor a cone of reals $x$, the reals of $\\mathrm{HOD}^{L[x]}$ are precisely the reals in $Q_3$, or equivalently, the set of reals in $M_1$, the minimal proper class mouse with a Woodin cardinal. We show that if $z$ is any real coding $M_1|δ^{+M_1}$, then $z$ is the base of such a cone (so $M_1^{#}$ is such a base). We also establish a kind of optimality for this result, by identifying a real $x$ such that $M_1\\subseteq L[x]$ but $\\mathbb{R}\\cap\\mathrm{HOD}^{L[x]}\\not\\subseteq M_1$, although there is a base for the cone in a generic extension of $L[x]$. We prove analogous results for $M_{2n}(x)$ for all $n$, with the optimality result holding for all $n$.\n\nDegree profiles of uniform polynomial consequences: Linear lower bounds for Nullstellensatz and Polynomial Calculus\n\nSøren Riis\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Wang_D in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?page=1&q=au%3AWang_D+in%3Amath)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; @misc{2608.18551, author = {Qi Liu and Dijian Wang and Shicai Gong}, title = {{M}inimizing the number of edges in $\\mathcal{{C}}